WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.413
Who owns each kind?

2
00:00:01.413 --> 00:00:04.673
The Compliance Automation
and Day-Two Operations

3
00:00:04.673 --> 00:00:07.700
book uses the roles it
already has, and adds none.

4
00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:10.819
An incident belongs to the
service desk supervisor,

5
00:00:10.819 --> 00:00:12.850
as service health is routed today.

6
00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:17.856
Maintenance belongs to the platform
owner of the affected platform:

7
00:00:17.856 --> 00:00:23.125
the cloud platform owner for Azure, AWS,
Google Cloud and each O C I tenancy,

8
00:00:23.125 --> 00:00:26.550
and the collaboration
owner for Microsoft 365.

9
00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:31.152
A retirement belongs to the system owner
of each affected system, who decides

10
00:00:31.152 --> 00:00:35.538
the schedule, and the platform owner
does the work through a normal change.

11
00:00:35.538 --> 00:00:39.928
A change is proposed by the platform
owner and authorized by the

12
00:00:39.928 --> 00:00:44.401
change advisory board, after the
ISSO's security impact analysis.

13
00:00:44.401 --> 00:00:47.737
Security notices belong
to security operations.

14
00:00:47.737 --> 00:00:52.149
And an advisory belongs to the platform
owner of the platform it names.

15
00:00:52.149 --> 00:00:55.938
Two decisions have no owner yet,
and the book doesn't invent one:

16
00:00:55.938 --> 00:00:59.058
who receives each provider's
notices at the source,

17
00:00:59.058 --> 00:01:03.860
and who reviews the contingency plan when
a notice names a system's resources.
